* the animation subsystem is Clay's transitions (see "Animation" in
  docs/vue-graphics-stack.md): the button highlights and the tool panels
  use it; popup windows (menus) cannot, they are separate SDL windows
* the printer dialog offers the options lpoptions reports (paper size,
  two-sided, color); orientation would need a rotation of the PDF
* the debug view (F1) shows the element tree; its own scroll bars and
  toggles are Clay's and are not styled like ours
* the main window receives the user icon bar (mask bit 16) and the
  interactive query line (prompt and input) and stores them, but
  vue_texmacs_widget_rep::do_layout never lays them out: neither is visible
* the colour picker offers named colours only; the bg flag, the patterns
  and the background images of the Qt picker are not implemented
* resize_widget ignores the initial scrolling position (hpos, vpos), and
  user_canvas_widget ignores its style

