DONE

* themes: every colour is a field of vue_theme, light and dark ship, the
  "gui theme" preference chooses and "default" follows the system
  (test theme, TEXMACS_VUE_THEME); the help balloons are a sheet of note
  paper instead of pure yellow
* themed vector icons: MuPDF draws the SVG sets of misc/pixmaps/light and
  misc/pixmaps/dark itself (no --with-resvg), sharp at every resolution and
  recoloured for the dark theme (test icons)
* the choice widgets honour their style (inert, grey, mini, monospaced,
  bold), test choice-style; the icons are loaded in the variant which
  matches the resolution instead of always the 2x one
* retina: each window follows the density of its display (with_window makes
  its factor current), the sizes are converted with retina_factor instead
  of a hardcoded 2, TEXMACS_VUE_DENSITY overrides it for testing
* drag and drop of files and text (test drop)
* the GUI entry points which were stubs: beep, image_gc,
  show_help_balloon, show_wait_indicator, external_event (test entrypoints)
* audit of the plugin (2026-09-21): lost clicks after the event batching,
  the renderer leak of every destroyed editor, dangling window pointers,
  the scroll requests dropped by a second layout pass, the file dialog
  callback running Scheme off the main thread, the hardcoded pixel
  density, unsigned pointer coordinates, a frame started re-entrantly
  from the event pump, two menus open at once; the traces are behind the
  debug flags and the plugin compiles without warnings
* the TeXmacs client/server works without Qt (System/Link/tm_sockets.cpp on
  the socket notifiers; both protocols tested: tests sockets, sockets-tls;
  the build has --with-gnutls)
* scroll bar thumbs, buttons and every element share button_logic
  (hot/active/capture: pressed, held, clicked); nothing stays hovered when
  the pointer leaves the window
* the Clay id strings are interned (the debug view read freed memory):
  the debug view works over any window (test debug-view)
* Clay transitions are driven by the frame time; button highlights fade
* typing goes through the text events (dead keys, input methods): a key
  which produces a character waits for its text
* printer dialog: printer, copies, pages and the printer's options
* tool panels slide in; the pre-edit of the input methods reaches the editor
* tests: color picker and printer (dialogs), splitters (aligned), keyboard
  focus between windows (focus-windows), debug view
* win->relayout removed (every window is laid out each iteration)
* no extra caching of the rendering structures (decision recorded in the docs)
* resize_widget min/max sizes are the limits of the window (set_size_limits)
* scrolling shifts the backing store of the editor and repaints only the
  exposed strips (scroll positions on the pixel grid)
* MuPDF renderer: plain fills and 1:1 picture blits write the pixels
  directly (the frame while scrolling was dominated by path rasterization
  and colorspace conversion)
* Clay's element hash map is pruned every frame (upstream Clay main since 2026-09-21):
  rebuilt widget trees no longer exhaust it (misdrawn tools after a refresh)
* the filtered choice list stays inside its box (input and long values clipped)
* embedded editors (texmacs-input): no bars for mask 0, they fill their
  resize box (the macro editors work)
* MuPDF renderer: pattern-filled glyphs, tiling patterns (resources fixed,
  images scaled to the requested size), neutral pattern behind the pages,
  missing images do not crash
* the editor is told when its viewport changes (notify_resizes) and centers
  the paper in a wider canvas; the paper follows the side tools
* section bars of the tools ("sections", "section-tabs") drawn as segmented
  bars and tabs; flat buttons are transparent
* widgets measured from the previous pass ask for another pass when new
  (layout_again), no misaligned first frame
* tabs/icon-tabs fill their container, the page area is as large as the largest
  page (hidden pages are measured off-screen), so switching tabs is stable
* menus stay in the window, scroll when taller than it and are drawn above
  the scroll bars of the editors; footer texts are clipped
* tab/shift-tab move the focus between the inputs of a dialog
* balloons are attached below their widget
* kinetic scrolling: wheel events scroll in sync, a launched wheel makes the
  view glide with a decaying velocity (editors and Clay containers); on
  macOS the trackpad gestures drag while the fingers are down and glide
  with the momentum of the system (SDL_HINT_MAC_SCROLL_MOMENTUM); the
  queued wheel/motion events of a frame are handled together
* editors are told when their window gains/loses the keyboard focus and when
  the focus moves to another widget (set_kbd_focus)
* menus and popups stay on the screen (flip, shift, clamp)
* resize_widget: default size for auto-sized windows, min/max as window limits
* implement commands in inputs_list_widget
* events go to the window they belong to (vue_input_state)
* auto-size dialog windows to their contents
* header dependencies in the makefile (-MMD)
* implement the missing widgets: popup/tooltip windows, popup_widget, tree view,
  ink, enum dropdown, (filtered) choice lists, extend, wait, empty, minibar,
  division, printer and color picker dialogs
* TEXMACS_VUE_SNAPSHOT=<dir> saves the rendering of each window as PNG (debugging)
* TEXMACS_VUE_SCRIPT=<file> drives the GUI with synthetic events (see tests/)
* popup windows grab the pointer (edit_mouse relies on the X11 grab semantics)
* implement copy & paste
* fix keyboard handling (Alt+3 should give #)
* remove balloons after a while
